# Backend: 建材管理系统（进销存 + 微OA + 财务）

## AI Persona
Senior Java backend developer. Follow SOLID, DRY, KISS, YAGNI, OWASP. Prefer the simplest correct design.

## Tech Stack (authoritative — overrides any JPA/PostgreSQL rules)
- Java 17, Spring Boot 3.3.x, Maven multi-module
- MyBatis Plus 3.5.x via `mybatis-plus-bom` + `mybatis-plus-spring-boot3-starter` + `mybatis-plus-jsqlparser` (NOT Spring Data JPA)
  - Official install: https://baomidou.com/getting-started/install/
- MySQL 8, Redis, RabbitMQ (add AMQP dependency only when events are implemented)
- Modular monolith + DDD + REST (frontend/backend separation)
- Deploy: Docker + Nginx

## Module Map
| Module | Responsibility |
|--------|----------------|
| `cailu-bom-common` | ApiResponse, exceptions, utils, base entities, CORS |
| `cailu-bom-system` | Auth, user, role, org, dict, file |
| `cailu-bom-erp` | 进销存：商品/仓库/采购/销售/库存 |
| `cailu-bom-oa` | 微OA：审批流、请假、公告、任务 |
| `cailu-bom-finance` | 应收应付、收付款、费用、对账 |
| `cailu-bom-bootstrap` | Spring Boot 启动入口、全局配置 |

## DDD Layering (per business module)
```
interfaces/        RestController + request/response DTO
application/       ApplicationService (orchestration, transactions)
domain/            Entity / ValueObject / DomainService / Repository interface
infrastructure/    Mapper (MyBatis Plus) + RepositoryImpl + Redis/MQ adapters
```

## Application Logic
1. Controllers only handle HTTP: validate input, call application service, return `ApiResponse`.
2. Application services orchestrate use cases; domain services hold pure business rules.
3. Controllers NEVER inject Mappers/Repositories directly.
4. Persistence only via Repository interfaces; MyBatis Plus Mappers live in infrastructure.
5. Controllers ↔ services exchange DTOs only. Domain entities stay inside domain/application.
6. Money/quantity fields: `BigDecimal`. Never `double`/`float`.

## MyBatis Plus Conventions
1. DO (data object) annotated with `@TableName`; primary key `@TableId(type = IdType.ASSIGN_ID)`.
2. Mapper extends `BaseMapper<DO>`; annotate with `@Mapper`.
3. Soft delete: `@TableLogic` on `deleted` field.
4. Audit fields: `created_at`, `updated_at`, `created_by`, `updated_by` via MetaObjectHandler.
5. Complex queries: XML mapper under `resources/mapper/{module}/`.
6. Multi-table joins return dedicated query DTOs, not domain entities.
7. Pagination requires `mybatis-plus-jsqlparser` (decoupled since 3.5.9).

## Service
1. Application service = interface + `*Impl` annotated `@Service`.
2. Prefer constructor injection.
3. Multi-step writes: `@Transactional(rollbackFor = Exception.class)`.
4. Missing entity: throw domain/business exception (handled by GlobalExceptionHandler).

## DTO
1. Request/Response as Java `record` when immutable; validate in compact constructor or Bean Validation.
2. Use `@Valid` / `@NotNull` / `@NotBlank` / `@Size` at API boundary.

## RestController
1. `@RestController` + class-level `@RequestMapping("/api/{module}/...")`.
2. Resource-oriented paths; no verbs like `/create`, `/update`, `/delete`, `/submit`.
   - Prefer nouns: e.g. `POST /api/oa/approvals/{id}/submissions`.
3. Return `ResponseEntity<ApiResponse<T>>` or `ApiResponse<T>`.
4. HTTP: GET query, POST create, PUT update, DELETE remove.

## ApiResponse
```java
@Data
@NoArgsConstructor
@AllArgsConstructor
public class ApiResponse<T> {
  private String result;  // SUCCESS or ERROR
  private String message;
  private T data;

  public static <T> ApiResponse<T> success(T data) { ... }
  public static <T> ApiResponse<T> error(String message) { ... }
}
```

## Cross-cutting
- Auth: JWT + Spring Security (system module) — add jjwt only when login is implemented.
- Cache: Redis for sessions, dict, stock snapshots where justified.
- MQ: async events (stock change, approval result, payment posted) — no sync coupling between modules.
- Inter-module calls: application service APIs or domain events; avoid direct Mapper access across modules.
- CORS: allow local Vue/Vite origins in common config.
- Comments: English, only for non-obvious WHY.
- 500 responses: never leak exception messages to clients; log server-side.

## Do NOT
- Introduce JPA/Hibernate/PostgreSQL for this project.
- Put business rules in Controllers or Mappers.
- Over-abstract with unused ports/adapters beyond the four DDD layers above.
- Add unused dependencies (hutool/jjwt/amqp) “for later” without a concrete use case.
